course: dictionary
lesson: 2569
title: Words from stories: dell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dell is a small valley or hollow, usually with trees and grass around it. It is a low, sheltered spot where the land dips down, so you may not see it until you are close.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows the Rat describes a dell «where the ground seems all hilly and humpy and hummocky». The bumpy, uneven ground is a clue: the land goes up and down, and the dip is hidden among the trees.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A small valley where the ground seems all hilly and humpy» still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A dell is a small valley or hollow, usually with trees and grass around it.
fact: Stories and poems often put a dell in a quiet, sheltered, pretty place.
fact: «The farmer's in his dell» is a nursery rhyme and a playground singing game.
fact: Dell is also a family name and the name of a computer company, and as a name it starts with a capital letter.
fact: A valley is a stretch of low land between hills, and a hollow is any low place where the ground dips.
exercise: In the Rat's words, what kind of ground does a dell have? | Covered in water like a lake | Hard and made of stone | *Hilly and humpy, with dips and bumps | Flat and smooth like a football pitch
exercise: What is a dell? | *A small valley or hollow, usually with trees and grass around it | A busy road with cars | A tall mountain covered in snow | A large lake in the middle of a city
exercise: Which place is most likely to be a dell? | A sandy beach by the sea | A tall glass office block | A shop on a high street | *A grassy hollow in a wood, with trees all round
test: In the nursery rhyme, the farmer is in his dell. Where is he? | On a ship at sea | In the middle of a busy town | Up in the sky | *Down in a small, grassy valley
test: Which words in the definition show that a dell is low ground? | *Hollow and valley | Cold and icy | Tall and rocky | Bright and loud
exam: How can you tell whether «dell» means a valley or a name in a text? | Guess, because both meanings are the same | Ignore the sentence and check only the spelling | Always pick the first meaning you read | *Look at the clues: a place with trees and grass means a valley, and a person or company means a name
